To use:

1. copy feeder-stats.pl & diablo-stats.sh (or cyclone-stats.sh if you are
   running Cyclone) to your bin directory
2. edit diablo-stats.sh (or cyclone-stats.sh) to match your site requirements
3. check that feeder-stats.pl '#!/path/perl' points to your copy of Perl5
4. if you want graphs (PNG-format) you'll need the Chart and GD perl modules:
   http://www.perl.com/CPAN/modules/by-module/GD/
   http://www.perl.com/CPAN/modules/by-module/Chart/
   (or get them at the nearest CPAN mirror)
5. copy the feeder-stats.conf to your /news directory
6. copy the logo.gif file to your $HtmlDir directory or put your own
   (not too big) logo.gif there.
7. install a crontab job to run diablo-stats.sh (or cyclone-stats.sh):
   ie.  59 * * * * /usr/local/bin/diablo-stats.sh > /dev/null 2>&1

Top1000 rank:

   feeder-stats shows the position of a feed in the Top1000 list
   (https://top1000.anthologeek.net/) next to its name.  The list is the
   file 'current' in the directory given with -T (default /news/top1000).
   diablo-stats.sh fetches it daily with top1000-fetch.sh (needs curl,
   fetch or wget; set TOP1000URL empty in diablo-stats.sh to turn this
   off), so copy top1000-fetch.sh to your bin directory as well.  A feed
   gets the best rank among the path names in the list that match its host
   name or one of the 'alias' lines of its label in dnewsfeeds: put the
   path name the peer uses in a Path: header there.  Hosts that are not in
   the list are left blank; -v tells which ones.  'sh test-top1000.sh' in
   this directory checks all of this on made-up data.

